  "worked_solution": "To predict the number of hours a person sleeps after watching TV for $6$ hours, we need to substitute $x=6$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =10-1.25x \\\\  & =10-1.25(6) \\\\  & =10-7.5 \\\\  & =2.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, a person watching TV for $6$ hours sleeps for approximately $2.5$ hours.\n\nNote: The point where $x=6$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
